          "model_answer": "<ol><li><strong>Quick Check:</strong> The USA operated as a liberal democracy with free, multi-party elections, freedom of speech, and constitutional civil rights. In contrast, the USSR was a totalitarian one-party state governed exclusively by the Communist Party (CPSU), where political dissent was outlawed, media was strictly censored, and the secret police (NKVD/KGB) eliminated opposition.</li><li><strong>Hinge Question:</strong> Capitalist ideology required free trade, private property, and open international markets to thrive, while Marxist-Leninist ideology taught that capitalism was an inherently exploitative system destined to collapse and that communism must actively spread worldwide. Each superpower saw the other's existence as an existential, irreconcilable threat to its own survival.</li></ol>"
