          "Source C": "Dr. Trâm’s diary was saved from burning by an American intelligence officer who was told by his translator: 'Do not burn this, it already has fire in it.' It gives an extraordinary, deeply human voice to the Vietnamese fighters who endured relentless American bombing. **Hinge Question:** How does reading a young Vietnamese doctor’s private diary challenge the one-sided view of the Vietnam War often shown in Western movies?",
