            "primer": "Compare armed deterrence across the NATO/Warsaw Pact frontier in Europe with devastating hot wars fought across Asia, Africa, and Latin America between 1945 and 1991.",
            "question": "Why does calling 1945–1991 a \"Cold War\" make sense from the perspective of London or Berlin, yet seem deeply misleading from the perspective of Seoul, Hanoi, or Kabul?"
